 "cfo_summary": [
  "<strong>Total available cash is $97,139</strong> across all nine entities, against a true bank balance of $319,102. The gap is $221,963 in uncleared transactions, the largest of the year. After <strong>$38,471 in external payments</strong> and <strong>$30,571 in intercompany management fees</strong>, projected end of week is <strong>$58,668</strong>.",
  "<strong>GRP projects to negative $17,586.</strong> True bank is $34,280 but uncleared transactions of $61,506 pull available to negative $27,226 before a single bill is paid. The August management fees of $30,571 land this week and are already in the projection. This is the same pending transaction pattern that ran six consecutive weeks from June 19 through July 24 and cleared on July 31. It is back after one clean week. Identify the source before next Thursday.",
  "<strong>Countryside carries $50,672 in uncleared payments</strong> against $109,055 true bank, leaving $58,383 available. Countryside remains the only viable funding source for a GRP transfer. It is also the entity holding the portfolio together: January through July it gained $62,435 in cash with zero home sales.",
  "<strong>Riverside projects to $1,108</strong> after $8,802 in payments, driven by $4,500 of Whitley tree work. Group Group sits at $87 for the fourth time in six weeks. Both are below any workable floor and neither has incoming funds this week.",
  "<strong>The nine week forecast does not go short.</strong> Low point is $136,593 the week of 9/25. Weekly timing now comes from eight weeks of actual cash flow rather than an even split, and the shape it reveals is that weeks two and three of every month are the pressure points. Mortgage interest lands in those weeks and the Group Group distribution falls in week three. Only one confirmed sale sits in the window, WW:3G at $2,000, with three more totaling $42,500 identified but outside 60 days.",
  "<strong>Home Tracker lien amounts are still blank across all 47 homes.</strong> Until that column is populated no net proceeds figure can be produced, so the forecast shows sale income with no offsetting lien payment. The 8/3 Ops Review gives the pattern: FS2:056 at $25,000 against a $19,734 lien nets $5,000 to $6,000. That calculation is needed for every home in the pipeline."
 ],
 "for_ownership": {
  "label": "Projected end-of-week cash",
  "number": 58667.97,
  "paragraph": "We close this week at roughly $58,700 available across all accounts after $38,500 in bills and $30,600 in management fees moving between our own entities. The number looks low because we are carrying an unusually large amount of payments that have not yet cleared the bank. Actual money in the accounts is $319,000. Golden Rule Practices is showing negative again after one clean week, and that is the item to resolve. Over the next sixty days the business covers itself, with the tightest point around $137,000 in late September. The middle of each month is when cash works hardest. Four homes are lined up to sell and none are confirmed inside that window, so any closing is upside."
 },
